You can stop a multi-step tool-calling loop after 5 steps by tracking the step count and returning a final message when the limit is reached. Here's how to do it:

```ts
import { streamText } from 'ai';
import { z } from 'zod';

let stepCount = 0;
const MAX_STEPS = 5;

async function runWithStepLimit() {
  return streamText({
    model: yourModel,
    tools: {
      yourTool: {
        description: '...',
        parameters: z.object({ ... }),
        execute: async ({ ... }) => {
          stepCount++;
          if (stepCount >= MAX_STEPS) {
            return { result: "Maximum steps reached" }; // Final output
          }
          // Continue with tool logic...
        }
      }
    },
    async onStepFinish({ text }) {
      if (stepCount >= MAX_STEPS) {
        return { finish: 'stop' }; // Stop the stream
      }
      return { text };
    }
  });
}
```

Alternatively, if you're using `generateText`, you can implement similar logic in the tool's execute function to prevent further calls after 5 steps.

